        <p class="profile-detail-region">Culture · Europe</p>
        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Vikings</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Homeland</span><span class="info-stat-val"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scandinavia">Scandinavia</a>, in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a>; settlements in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-isles">British Isles</a>, Normandy, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/faroe-islands">Faroes</a>, Iceland and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greenland">Greenland</a> and along the rivers of present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a></span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">c. 793–1066, from the raid on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lindisfarne">Lindisfarne</a> to the death of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harald-hardrada">Harald Hardrada</a> at Stamford Bridge; raiding at its height in the 9th century, kingdoms and conversion in the 10th and 11th</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Known for</span><span class="info-stat-val">Longships; raids and tribute; the settlement of Iceland and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greenland">Greenland</a> and the voyages to Vinland; trading towns and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> hoards; runestones and sagas</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">How we know them</span><span class="info-stat-val">The chronicles of their victims and neighbours (the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anglo-saxon-chronicle">Anglo-Saxon Chronicle</a>, the Annals of St Bertin, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/annals-of-ulster">Annals of Ulster</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/primary-chronicle">Primary Chronicle</a>, Arabic writers such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahmad-ibn-fadlan">Ibn Fadlan</a>); runic inscriptions; Icelandic sagas written down from the 13th century; excavated sites such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hedeby">Hedeby</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/birka">Birka</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/york">York</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lanse-aux-meadows">L’Anse aux Meadows</a>; the Oseberg and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gokstad-ship">Gokstad ships</a></span></div>
        </div>
